47:48.720 --> 48:01.760
I actually have an observation on an earlier comment, one-time verification of the Squash

48:01.760 --> 48:07.780
FS is not good enough, while Squash FS itself is read-only, it does not cache all your data.

48:07.780 --> 48:12.480
So if you're sneaky, you can go in and rewrite the data that's in the Squash FS.

48:12.480 --> 48:17.060
We found this because one of our clients accidentally ran their upgrade system against their currently

48:17.060 --> 48:18.820
running SquashFS.

48:18.820 --> 48:22.820
This makes the kernel very unhappy and crashes the system.

